hanism illustration, not the selected or an extra test-tuned model. Some classes have no test support.</p></section><section id="3"><small>EXPERIMENT 3</small><h2>Non-exhaustive overlapping K-Means</h2><p><b>Question.</b> Which images receive zero, one or multiple cluster memberships?</p><p><b>Method.</b> K=20 on all 1,641 saved normalized vectors; Euclidean objective, unnormalized means. NumPy translation of Whang’s released MATLAB data implementation: cover N−round(βN) nearest images, then globally assign round((α+β)N) remaining image-center pairs. Same converged ordinary K-Means initialization for the four settings. α=β=0 explicitly tested.</p><figure><a href="results/bioclip25_neo_counts.png"><img loading="lazy" src="results/bioclip25_neo_counts.png"></a><figcaption>Actual counts at four preset settings; overlap is partly required by the assignment budget.</figcaption></figure><details><summary>Exact counts for all encoders and settings</summary><table border="1" class="dataframe">
